# Keep the build context small and keep secrets OUT of the image.
#
# WHY WE ADD IT: you already know this file from Docker. Here it matters extra:
#   an image can be shared (registry, teammates). If config/master.key got copied
#   in by `COPY . .`, anyone with the image could read it. In Kubernetes the key
#   arrives at runtime from a Secret instead (see ../secrets.example.yaml).
# APP NAME: nothing here depends on the app name, so renaming the app changes nothing.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Secrets: never bake these into an image. They arrive at runtime from a Kubernetes Secret.
.env*
config/master.key
config/credentials/*.key

# Runtime junk
log/*
tmp/*
storage/*
!log/.keep
!tmp/.keep
!storage/.keep

# Not needed in production
node_modules
spec
test
coverage
.rspec
.rubocop.yml

# Docker files themselves
Dockerfile*
.dockerignore
